[h1]Starbase Solar System Exploitation (4.2+)[/h1]
A small mod for enhancing starbases so they can provide a greater economic boost to your empire and have a greater impact on the planets in system, inspired by some of the features of Stellaris Immortal.  Each one is unlocked by one of the standard technologies.

[h1]New Starbase/Orbital Ring Modules[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Mining Terminal:[/b]  Produces 6 minerals.  Boosted by the Mining Hub and Alloy Refinery buildings.
[*] [b]Research Terminal:[/b] Produces 3 of each research type.  Boosted by the Astrophysics, Astrogeology and Aerospace Labs.
[*] [b]Hydroponics Module:[/b] Starbases only.  Produces 5 food.
[/list]

[h1]New Starbase/Orbital Ring Resource Buildings[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Supercapacitor System:[/b] Produces 10 energy and 6 more for each Solar Panel Network on the station.  Increases the energy produced by all energy mining stations in system by 25%.
[*] [b]Mining Hub:[/b] Produces 10 minerals and 5 more for each Mining Terminal on the station.  Increases the minerals produced by all mining stations in system by 25%.
[*] [b]Alloy Refinery:[/b] Requires a mined alloy deposit in system.  Produces 5 alloys and 2 more for each Mining Terminal on the station.  Increases the alloys produced by all mining stations in system by 25%.
[*] [b]Astrophysics Lab:[/b]   Produces 5 physics research and 5 more for each Research Terminal on the station.  Increases the physics research produced by all research stations in system by 25%.  If the system contains an exploited dark matter deposit it also produces 1 dark matter.
[*] [b]Astrogeology Lab:[/b]  Produces 5 society research and 5 more for each Research Terminal on the station.  Increases the society research produced by all research stations in system by 25%.  If the system contains an exploited zro deposit it also produces 1 zro.
[*] [b]Aerospace Lab:[/b]  Produces 5 engineering research and 5 more for each Research Terminal on the station.  Increases the engineering research produced by all research stations in system by 25%.  If the system contains an exploited living metal deposit it also produces 1 living metal.
[*] [b]Food Processing Hub:[/b] Produces 5 food, plus 5 more for each habitable planet in system.
[*] [b]Strategic Resource Refineries:[/b] One each for exotic gases, volatile motes and rare crystals.  Requires an exploited deposit of the relevant resource in system.  Each produces 2 of its resoure on of the relevant mining stations in system by 25%.
[/list]

[h1]New Starbase System Enhancement Buildings[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Battle Stations:[/b] Increases the starbase's hull, armour and shields by 25%.
[*] [b]Revenue and Customs House:[/b] Produces 50 trade, plus 10 per level of your Trading Posts councilor, 10 per orbital ring trade hub in system and 5 per Trading Hub on the station.  Increases the trade nets in system by 25%.
[*] [b]Fulfillment Warehouse:[/b] Increases the amenities of all colonised planets in system by 20%.
[*] [b]Systemnet Comms Grid:[/b] Produces 10 unity, plus 10 per orbital ring bureaucracy hub in system.  Increases the unity produced by jobs and the happiness of all colonised planets in system by 10%.
[/list]

[h1]New Orbital Ring Buildings[/h1][list]
[*] [b]Orbital Research Hub:[/b] Gives +0.5 research to each physicist, biologist and engineer on the planet it orbits.
[/list]

[h1]FAQ[/h1]
[b]Building Module Bonuses Don't Show Up?[/b]
The building module bonuses get folded into the base value of the building.  If you check a building production before and then building production after the relevant module you'll see that the base value has jumped appropriately.

[b]Building X doesn't show up in the list?[/b]
Because the building list gets cluttered and bounces around when you select anything my bonus buildings only show when it is possible for them to be built.  So the Alloy foundry and exotic resource buildings will be completely hidden if there isn't a relevant deposit in the system.  Similarly the ones that enhance colonised planets will only show if there is a colonised planet.

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
No vanilla overrides, so will work fine with just about everything

Should play fine with mods that increase the number of buildings / modules on a starbase.
In the case of mods that also add similar modules and buildings (star base expanded/extended, NSC etc...) then they are unlikely to interact (my buildings won't recognise a starbase extended mining module) so it may get confusing.

